From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arjun C R <arjuncr@ami.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] utils: tolerate missing i3c-hub "tp_conf" on AST2700

The AST2700 mipi-i3c-hci i3c-hub sysfs does not expose a "tp_conf"
(target-port config) attribute, so readTargetPortConfig() threw and
I3CHub::init() aborted before publishing the hub object - the device on
a hub-capable bus never appeared on D-Bus. Return an empty config when
the attribute is absent so the hub is still exposed.

Upstream-Status: Pending [applied downstream for the intel-ast2700
MACHINE only; upstream should support the mipi-i3c-hci sysfs layout]
Signed-off-by: Arjun C R <arjuncr@ami.com>
---
 utils.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/utils.cpp b/utils.cpp
--- a/utils.cpp
+++ b/utils.cpp
@@ -342,6 +342,11 @@
 std::string readTargetPortConfig(const std::filesystem::path& devicePath)
 {
     auto tpConfigPath = devicePath / "tp_conf";
+    if (!std::filesystem::exists(tpConfigPath))
+    {
+        // AST2700's i3c-hub sysfs does not expose "tp_conf".
+        return "";
+    }
     std::string tpConfig = readFile(tpConfigPath);
     return tpConfig;
 }
